A||||6||FieroGTGirl||OK....Now Cruise Control||||5||
Z||000000||FieroGTGirl||05-07-2000||05:38 PM||||First of all thank to all who gave input for my windshield washer problem.  Turned out to be no problem at all(hoses from reservoir were kinked on both feeds..previous owner must have done this, don't know why)<P>On to the next problem...Cruise Control is totally dead what do I look for first?<P>Thanks Guys...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-07-2000||05:55 PM||||There is a switch under the brake/clutch that disengages the cruise, when those peddles are pushed.  I've had intermittant problems with the switch being activated and the cruise shuts off.  The other obvious is the cruise stalk switch (Fiero store $83), or the cruise solinoid in the engine compartment.  Some one had a used one on ebay for $10. <BR> I had replaced the stalk, but the problem still exists, now its down to the brake/clutch switch.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Robert||05-07-2000||06:03 PM||||First I would look for a disconnected vacuum line to the curse control.  Look at the vacuum lines around the unit in the engine compartment.  Check for cracks.  If someone else has dropped the cradle, they may not have reconnected the lines.  Good luck.<P>Robert<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||05-07-2000||06:57 PM||||There are 4 main parts in the cruise system on Fiero.<P>the stalk. The turn signal stalk is a standard GM part, available from many sources. GM installed a fairly large batch of junk ones in a whole bunch of cars. mainly 85-86 modles. (there was a TSB on it. It said do the obvious and replace the stalk.)<P>The clutch/brake switches. These kill the cruise if ether is activated.<P>the cruise unit. this is a seperate part on most Fiero. It is built into the ECM on 87-88 4 cylinder.<P>the cruise servo. This is a vacuum operated device. check the vacuum lines and the vacuum reserve can. (looks like a can or a grapefruit size plasic ball.) I list this last but check it first. The metal can version of the vacuum reserve tends to rot out. You can get the plastic ones in any scrap yard.||||reg||4
Z||000004||AL||05-07-2000||07:08 PM||||hey girl, go to the junkyard pull one out of any gm car that looks like yours and hook it up to yours, my gt had the same problem it turned ot to be the stalk, also check hoses on the can in the back disconnect one hose and blow in it if you don't here any air comming out of the can it will be the stalk. they only cost 5 to 10 bucks at the junkyard, good luck princessa( princess in spanish)||||reg||1
Z||000005||mshill||05-07-2000||10:36 PM||||I also have a non-functional cruise control on my 86SE.  I have several (3) stalks that I have tested with my ohm meter and they all look good.  My vacuum canister holds vacuum because when I disconnect one of the lines it releases all the vacuum.  I have swapped out the vacuum solenoid with the one from my GT and checked that the brake and clutch swithes were working properly.  I guess that only leaves the control unit (under the carpet, drivers side console).  I am goin to try to switch it, but I have heard these rarely go bad.  Anything else?||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroGTGirl||05-07-2000||11:21 PM||||Thanks I will check it out!||||reg||1
